rite_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":70558.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":2103.0,"requests":5}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify an operator-visible signal (log/metric) emitted when repair_at_write_boundary completes a retirement and when completion fails, so a stuck retry loop is observable.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.45,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'On completion failure, preserve the overlap for retry.'","No mention of any log/metric/trace emitted on completion or on failure anywhere in Plan, Testing, or Acceptance Criteria."],"finding":"The plan adds a new write-bearing completion path (retirement completion at the reconcile boundary) and a failure branch, but specifies no observability (log/metric/trace) for either the successful completion or the completion failure. On completion failure the plan preserves the overlap for retry but does not surface the failure to operators, so a persistently-failing retirement completion would silently recur every pass with no operator-visible signal.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb23cd3bf8493a8e1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 4 / Outcome","norm_id":"n6a6d93b7ceac7ba7","priority":0.5,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A retirement completion repeatedly fails under-lock; the overlap is preserved and retried every reconcile pass, but operators have no log/metric to notice the stuck state."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the persist/scoped guard belongs in the recovery layer (not the caller like `recover_pending_bindings`); if the choice is only to save reconcile.py lines, note that the T1 recovery convention places this decision at the caller.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.752,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["run_differs.py:415 `if not scoped_ids:` guards `recover_pending_bindings` at the caller","binding_recovery.py:285-287: 'whether recovery runs at all is the CALLER's decision (run_differs skips it for a scoped pass)'","Plan step 1 moves the guard into `BindingRecovery.repair_at_write_boundary`, exposed through the facade","Plan justifies the move by the reconcile.py 800-line cap and RP-04 co-editing the file"],"finding":"The new `repair_at_write_boundary(*, persist, scoped)` guard pushes the persist/scoped run-or-skip decision INTO the recovery/facade layer, whereas the sibling recovery operation `recover_pending_bindings` guards at the caller and its docstring explicitly declares the caller owns that decision — a layering divergence for the identical concern.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f09627480065f8710","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1; binding_recovery.py:285-287 and run_differs.py:415","norm_id":"nd037ad2adeb37ee5","priority":0.198,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future reader comparing the two recovery entry points sees two different conventions for the same persist/scoped decision"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Clarify that the placement 'after the staleness gate, before the first fetch' is a positional insertion (between reconcile.py:283 and :329), noting that ensure_selection_current is scoped-only and does not execute on the unscoped write-bearing path the guard actually runs on.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.402,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Context: 'Retirement completion is safe only after provider preflight and exclusive pass ownership succeed and under-lock staleness validation passes'","reconcile.py:282-283: 'if selection_ids: ensure_selection_current(selection_ids, local_tickets)' — the gate is scoped-only","The guard runs when 'not scoped', i.e. selection_ids is empty, so ensure_selection_current does not fire on the path recovery actually completes on"],"finding":"The plan's precondition framing ('safe only after ... under-lock staleness validation passes', AC1) describes a data dependency that does not execute in the target case: ensure_selection_current (the staleness gate) runs only when selection_ids is truthy (reconcile.py:282), but the operation is guarded to run precisely when the pass is unscoped (not scoped), so an unscoped write-bearing pass never traverses that gate. The insertion point is positionally correct regardless, but the stated ordering rationale conflates a positional 'after line 283' with a semantic 'after the gate validated', which for the write-bearing/unscoped case is a no-op gate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff4f2ae16e2b3f0a3","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Acceptance Criteria AC1 / Plan step 2","norm_id":"n14a05eeee394dd2d","priority":0.198,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer wiring an assertion that recovery observes a validated-staleness state on the unscoped write-bearing pass finds no such validation ran, and may add a spurious dependency or mis-order the call."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Reword the ordering rationale to state the call sits between the selection-staleness gate (scoped-only) and the first remote fetch inside _load_snapshots, and that for the unscoped write-bearing pass the guarded call is the first write-boundary action after binding-store load.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile T2's ordering clause with parent Step 3: either state completion also precedes the write-bearing sync-log artifact (moving the call/guard so it does not depend on the post-artifact `scoped_ids`), or explicitly record that the binding boundary is 'before first remote observation' (parent AC1) and the sync-log artifact is intentionally excluded — and align the parent Step 3 wording accordingly.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.652,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Parent Step 3: 'Invoke completion once ... immediately after the under-lock staleness validation and before the pass creates any write-bearing artifact, fetches remote issue state, walks bindings, diffs, or mutates